  "description": "After a KERI 2.0 inception, an attachments group holds a first-seen replay couples group (-O) of one couple: a sequence number with code 0A (16 bytes, 24 characters) and a datetime with code 1AAG (a four-character code, 36 characters). The datetime's 32 characters are the ISO-8601 text with ':' written 'c', '.' written 'd' and '+' written 'p', keripy's rendering of the 'custom encoded' form the master table names but does not define; only its encoding as a primitive matters here.",
